{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779484582,"nonce":"Z1CfbTMo0aWb6J415vBNd0O1RMk=","message":"## Cross-reference: recurrent-edge Studio UX and stateful-node inspection\n\nNew Studio-facing issue: `7f02d30` — Studio recurrent-edge UX and stateful-node inspector.\n\nDecision for Studio interaction:\n\n- When a user creates an edge that closes a directed cycle, the newly dropped edge should become the recurrent/time-cut edge by default.\n- Recurrent edges should be visibly distinct from ordinary same-step wires and should expose their init/status in the properties panel.\n- Opened subgraphs should prefer explicit recurrent edges for hidden recurrence, e.g. GRU/LSTM hidden loops, rather than replacing those edges with always-visible state-slot projections.\n- Stateful nodes may have a small non-text cue on the canvas, but state details belong in the selected-node properties panel to avoid visual clutter.\n\nRelated core issue: `f93db6a` covers backend/schema recurrence semantics. Deferred future design: `56dfd97` covers intentional inner-rollout/multirate subgraphs, which should not block the near-term recurrent-edge UX.","files":null}]}